{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>On the twenty-fourth [day]</b> — Rabbi Yeshua said: that this is the ninth from the start of Darius's reign, and we do not know when the beginning of the month of his reign was. And he did not speak accurately, for behold it is written in the prophecy of Zechariah, in the ninth month, Kislev, and behold the count is from Nisan, and so the month of Ziv is the month of Iyyar, for \"the second month\" is not attached to the beginning of Solomon's reign but rather [the word] \"reign\" is attached to \"in the fourth year,\" for it is not the custom of Israel to count months but only years, and so it is: \"in the fourth year of Solomon's reign over Israel, in the month of Ziv, which is the second month,\" which is Iyyar."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:30.270604123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}